+## S4 CrisisEngine (GDD § M5, ADR-4, FORGE #3 — fair + predictable crises).
+##
+## Downstream of the flow: reads Topology + PacketFlow state, produces warnings +
+## CrisisEvents. NEVER owns/drives the demand timeline (that's the director's job,
+## upstream — a crisis is a CONSEQUENCE of topology + flow, never its own cause).
+## Every CrisisEvent carries a root_cause (§10.1.3) — fleshed in S4 (E4.1-E4.3).
+##
+## S0 scope: evaluate() returns a report carrying the director's forecast (so the
+## View can show the "weather report") but raises no warnings/crises yet.
+## Pure RefCounted (ADR-1); deterministic (trivially, while empty).
+class_name CrisisEngine
+extends RefCounted
+
+var catalogs: GameCatalogs = null
+var balance: BalanceData = null
+
+
+func _init(p_catalogs: GameCatalogs = null, p_balance: BalanceData = null) -> void:
+	catalogs = p_catalogs
+	balance = p_balance
+
+
+func evaluate(tick: int, _topology: TopologySnapshot, _flow: PacketFlow,
+			  era_id: int, director: ScriptedDirector) -> CrisisReport:
+	var report := CrisisReport.new()
+	report.tick = tick
+	# Surface the director's forecast (set-pieces within their lead time) so the
+	# View can render the "weather report" panel (sprint-plan §3.4, P3 fairness).
+	if director != null:
+		report.forecast = director.forecast_for_era(era_id, tick)
+	# E4.1-E4.3 (S4): compute strain metrics, raise WarningSigns, fire fair crises
+	# each carrying a root_cause + preventive_redesign (§10.1.3, AC-E13).
+	return report
